let the page veto the unread state of a message

An ignore list living in the page can hide a bot's lines, but the buffer still lights
up and the unread count still grows on messages nobody will read — and a desktop
notification still fires.

One hook, asked before the unread state is raised: the message is still received and
stored, only the unread state is dropped.

diff --git a/components/app.js b/components/app.js
index fae1f4d..c0ebe1e 100644
--- a/components/app.js
+++ b/components/app.js
@@ -784,6 +784,12 @@ export default class App extends Component {
 				msgUnread = Unread.MESSAGE;
 			}
 
+			// The page can veto: a sender it ignores should not light up the buffer, nor
+			// notify. The message still arrives and is stored, only the unread state drops.
+			if (window.gamjaSkipUnread && window.gamjaSkipUnread(msg)) {
+				msgUnread = Unread.NONE;
+			}
+
